; ACCEPTANCE: the JavaScript surface is declarable, and the declaration is
; unchecked and under-informed. Every line here is GENERATED by
; gauntlet/stdlib/js.go from the runtime itself.
;
; THE OTHER TWO SURVEYS ASK "CAN WE DECLARE IT" AND "CAN WE USE IT". Neither
; question has content on this host: `targets/js` declares every type `any`, so
; declarability is 100% BY CONSTRUCTION and the obtainable-type fixed point has
; one type in its domain. So what a JavaScript declaration actually needs is a
; NAME, a CALL FORM and an ARITY — and this program exercises all three, with the
; third one failing on purpose.
;
;   Math.max        the host reports arity 2 and the function is VARIADIC. Two
;                   arguments is what the declaration can say, and two arguments
;                   is what a program gets. `(Math.max 3 7)` is 7.
;
;   String.toUpperCase   an INSTANCE member, reached through `.prototype.` in the
;                   manifest and declared with the receiver as argument 0 — the
;                   convention Win32's `HANDLE` used and gomethods-2026-09-09
;                   generalised. Our `string` IS a JavaScript string, so no
;                   coercion is needed and none is emitted.
;
;   path.join       AND THIS IS THE FINDING, made concrete rather than argued.
;                   `path.join.length` is 0, so the generated declaration takes
;                   NO ARGUMENTS: `(prim join (none) any expr "path.join()")`.
;                   The declaration is legal, it builds, it runs, and it cannot
;                   be passed a path. `path.join()` returns ".", which is what
;                   this prints.
;
; THE HOST DOES NOT MERELY DECLINE TO GIVE US TYPES — IT MISREPORTS THE SHAPE.
; `Function.length` counts the parameters before the first default or rest, and
; a native function's parameters are not introspectable at all: `Math.max.length`
; is 2, `console.log.length` is 0, `Array.prototype.map.length` is 1. A
; declaration must name an arity and nothing on this host can check it, which is
; overloading.md's `Println`/`Println2`/`Println3` arriving as the only honest
; shape — one declaration per arity a program actually uses.
;
; It prints 7, then ABC, then a single dot.

(use js/global/Math as Math)
(use js/global/String as Str)
(use js/path as path)
(use io)

(export main)

(def main ()
  (seq
    (io.print-int (Math.max 3 7))
    (io.print-line (Str.toUpperCase "abc"))
    (io.print-line (path.join))))
